<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ratan Singh of Bundi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 1607–1631</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ratan Singh was Rao of Bundi, a Hada <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chauhan">Chauhan</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajputs">Rajput</a> state in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajasthan">Rajasthan</a>, from 1607 to 1631, and a commander in the service of the Mughal emperors. He fought for them in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deccan">Deccan</a> and was rewarded with high rank. After his death <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shah-jahan">Shah Jahan</a> granted Kota to his son Madho Singh, founding the separate state of Kotah, while Bundi passed to his grandson <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chhatrasal">Chhatrasal</a>.</p></div>
